preConditionHook:
// LINDA RASCHKE'S ORIGINAL "ANTI", the confirmation Grimes cites beside his own
// price-structure Anti: a FAST stochastic is rising while a SLOW one is falling
// (mirrored) -- two time frames' momentum sloping against each other.
//
// WAS PRIORITY C, RESOLVED: the register's `stochastic` row is VERIFIED and
// covers the whole chain, and StochasticCross is the measured port this rule
// copies. Not a duplicate of it -- that rule fires on a SlowK/SlowD cross at
// ONE length and never compares two lengths; this one never reads SlowD.
//
// WHICH OUTPUT: the merged pseudocode spells the series fastK(n); the reading
// taken here is SlowK, deliberately (the ratio of sums is the VERIFIED
// quantity, Raschke's Anti is a slow-stochastic rule, and a one-bar slope on a
// 5-bar raw FastK is close to a coin flip). Recorded, not hidden.
//
// SMOOTHING: only the first smoothing argument reaches SlowK -- SlowD is never
// read here -- so smoothing1 is passed in both of the EasyLanguage call's
// smoothing slots rather than carrying an input that could not change
// behaviour. SmoothingType is pinned to 1, the only measured type.
//
// MEASURED CHAIN (the `stochastic` row, VERIFIED, EL_Stochastic_Probe.txt):
//   oFastK = 100*(C - LL(Length)) / (HH - LL)   -- fresh, real price history;
//   oSlowK = oFastD = 100*Sum(C - LL, Smoothing1) / Sum(HH - LL, Smoothing1),
//            a RATIO OF SUMS, NOT an average of FastK (refuted at maxd 24);
//   WARM-UP IS SEED-FILLED, NOT ZERO-FILLED: the num/den series exist only
//   from the study's first calculated bar, and a short sum pads its missing
//   terms with the FIRST bar's value. The growing vectors below reproduce
//   that: they start empty at the first evaluated bar and never see pre-study
//   bars. Sums run NEWEST-FIRST, the EL Summation order.
// An all-flat window across the whole sum makes a denominator 0; EL raises
// there and this mirror does not guard either, as StochasticCross does not.
//
// All scratch is declared in localVariables, never at hook scope: the
// generator only prefixes declared locals, so a hook-scope declaration is a
// redefinition when this rule is placed twice in one strategy.
//
// ---- FAST CHAIN, length fastLookback ----
hhWin = high[0];
llWin = low[0];
for (int i = 1; i < (int)fastLookback; ++i) {
    if (el_gt(high[i], hhWin)) { hhWin = high[i]; }
    if (el_lt(low[i], llWin)) { llWin = low[i]; }
}
fNumHist.push_back(close[0] - llWin);
fDenHist.push_back(hhWin - llWin);
sumN = 0.0;
sumD = 0.0;
have = (int)fNumHist.size();
take = (int)smoothing1;
if (have < take) { take = have; }
for (int i = 0; i < take; ++i) {
    sumN += fNumHist[fNumHist.size() - 1 - i];
    sumD += fDenHist[fDenHist.size() - 1 - i];
}
miss = (int)smoothing1 - take;
if (miss > 0) {
    sumN += miss * fNumHist[0];
    sumD += miss * fDenHist[0];
}
fSlowK = 100.0 * sumN / sumD;
// ---- SLOW CHAIN, length slowLookback ----
hhWin = high[0];
llWin = low[0];
for (int i = 1; i < (int)slowLookback; ++i) {
    if (el_gt(high[i], hhWin)) { hhWin = high[i]; }
    if (el_lt(low[i], llWin)) { llWin = low[i]; }
}
sNumHist.push_back(close[0] - llWin);
sDenHist.push_back(hhWin - llWin);
sumN = 0.0;
sumD = 0.0;
have = (int)sNumHist.size();
take = (int)smoothing1;
if (have < take) { take = have; }
for (int i = 0; i < take; ++i) {
    sumN += sNumHist[sNumHist.size() - 1 - i];
    sumD += sDenHist[sDenHist.size() - 1 - i];
}
miss = (int)smoothing1 - take;
if (miss > 0) {
    sumN += miss * sNumHist[0];
    sumD += miss * sDenHist[0];
}
sSlowK = 100.0 * sumN / sumD;
// The one-bar slopes read the EL VARIABLES' own history, zero-filled before
// the strategy's first evaluated bar -- mirrored by prevFSlowK / prevSSlowK,
// which start at 0 and are advanced in endOfFileHook so the value read here is
// always the previous bar's (MonthlyProfitTarget's idiom). On that first bar
// "rising" is measured against 0 and neither AND can hold. Mirrored, not
// corrected.
// A ratio of price DIFFERENCES, so the whole rule passes the shift test.
